{#
settings/_ai.html.twig
─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
What this person wants from the assistant: which of the three features they
use, what the composer should know about them, and how much of a conversation
it hands the model.

THE THREE ROWS ARE A CENSUS OF AiFeature, NOT A HAND-KEPT LIST
The rows come from SettingsController::aiSectionData(), which maps
AiFeature::cases() — so a fourth feature appears here without this template
changing, and AiPreferencesTest counts `data-ai-feature` against the enum for
exactly that reason.

A feature the ADMINISTRATOR has not switched on renders as a row with no
control and a muted line saying so. That is the ceiling made visible: a switch
that silently does nothing is worse than no switch, and the row still has to be
there, or somebody looking for the feature concludes plMail does not have it.

WHAT THESE SETTINGS ARE ABOUT
Usefulness and speed. plMail talks to a model on the operator's own network, so
none of this is a choice about where mail goes — it is a choice about which
features are worth having and how much time a draft may spend. The context
control is the one to read that way: more of the conversation is a better
reply and a longer wait on a GPU the indexer is also queueing for.

THREE PEER CARDS, not one card with three bands — the rule index.html.twig
states at the General section: each of these is a section-grade subject with
its own heading and subheading in the catalogue.

Variables:
  aiFeatures      list of { key, icon, adminOn, enabled }
  aiReplyContext  ReplyContext — how much the composer reads
  aiAboutMe       string
  aiSystemPrompt  string
#}

{# _card.html.twig pads a body only when asked, because most bodies are lists
   that pad their own rows. These do — `px-4 py-3`, matching the insights card
   and the clock — and tests/e2e/settings-card-insets.spec.ts MEASURES the
   result rather than checking class names, so a card that forgets this fails
   there rather than merely looking wrong. #}
<div class="space-y-4">

    {% embed 'settings/_card.html.twig' with {
        heading:    'settings.ai.features.heading'|trans,
        subheading: 'settings.ai.features.subheading'|trans,
    } %}
        {% block body %}
            {# Set inside the block rather than at the top of the file: an
               {% embed %} block is compiled against the embedded template's
               context, so a `{% set %}` in the outer scope is not visible here
               and `strict_variables` would turn that into a 500. #}
            {% set segGroup = 'grid grid-flow-col auto-cols-fr w-28 shrink-0 rounded-pane border border-line overflow-hidden' %}
            {% set segText  = 'flex h-full items-center justify-center px-2 py-1.5 text-center text-[11px] leading-tight text-ink-muted
                               peer-checked:bg-accent peer-checked:text-accent-ink
                               peer-focus-visible:ring-2 peer-focus-visible:ring-inset peer-focus-visible:ring-accent
                               transition-colors' %}

            <div class="px-4 py-3 space-y-3"
                 data-controller="settings--toggle"
                 data-settings--toggle-url-value="{{ path('app_settings_ai_toggle') }}"
                 data-settings--toggle-token-value="{{ csrf_token('ai_preferences_toggle') }}">

                {% for feature in aiFeatures %}
                    {% set name = ('settings.ai.feature.' ~ feature.key)|trans %}
                    <div class="flex items-start justify-between gap-3"
                         data-ai-feature="{{ feature.key }}">
                        <span class="flex items-start gap-3 min-w-0">
                            <i class="{{ feature.icon }} w-4 text-zinc-400 mt-0.5 shrink-0" aria-hidden="true"></i>
                            <span class="min-w-0">
                                <span class="block text-xs font-medium text-ink-muted">{{ name }}</span>
                                <span class="block text-[11px] text-ink-faint mt-0.5">
                                    {{ ('settings.ai.feature.' ~ feature.key ~ '_hint')|trans }}
                                </span>
                            </span>
                        </span>

                        {% if feature.adminOn %}
                            <div class="{{ segGroup }}" role="radiogroup" aria-label="{{ name }}">
                                {% for on in [true, false] %}
                                    <label class="cursor-pointer">
                                        <input type="radio" name="ai-{{ feature.key }}" class="peer sr-only"
                                               value="{{ on ? '1' : '0' }}"
                                               data-key="{{ feature.key }}"
                                               data-action="change->settings--toggle#toggle"
                                               aria-label="{{ (on ? 'settings.ai.seg.on' : 'settings.ai.seg.off')|trans }}"
                                            {{ feature.enabled == on ? 'checked' : '' }}>
                                        <span class="{{ segText }}">
                                            {{ (on ? 'settings.ai.seg.on' : 'settings.ai.seg.off')|trans }}
                                        </span>
                                    </label>
                                {% endfor %}
                            </div>
                        {% else %}
                            {# No control at all rather than a disabled one. A
                               greyed switch invites a click that cannot do
                               anything; a sentence says who to ask. #}
                            <span class="shrink-0 w-28 text-[11px] leading-tight text-ink-faint text-right"
                                  data-ai-feature-admin-off>
                                {{ 'settings.ai.feature.admin_off'|trans }}
                            </span>
                        {% endif %}
                    </div>
                {% endfor %}
            </div>
        {% endblock %}
    {% endembed %}

    {% embed 'settings/_card.html.twig' with {
        heading:    'settings.ai.notes.heading'|trans,
        subheading: 'settings.ai.notes.subheading'|trans,
    } %}
        {% block body %}
            {#
            ONE form and ONE button for both fields, and deliberately not the
            auto-submit idiom the segments use. These two are typed rather than
            clicked and are read together when a draft is built, so a form that
            posted on every blur would send half-finished sentences — and would
            post the OTHER field's value alongside them, which is the
            shared-form problem _compose_behavior.html.twig warns about.

            data-turbo="false" like the other posting forms on this page: the
            action redirects, and the flash lands on the reload.
            #}
            <div class="px-4 py-3">
                <form method="post" action="{{ path('app_settings_ai_notes') }}" data-turbo="false" class="space-y-4">
                    <input type="hidden" name="_token" value="{{ csrf_token('settings-ai-notes') }}">

                    <div class="space-y-1.5">
                        <label for="settings-ai-about-me" class="block text-xs font-medium text-ink-muted">
                            {{ 'settings.ai.notes.about_me_label'|trans }}
                        </label>
                        <p class="text-[11px] text-ink-faint leading-snug">{{ 'settings.ai.notes.about_me_hint'|trans }}</p>
                        {# maxlength is the SAME constant the property hook
                           clamps to. Two copies of a limit is how a textarea
                           accepts four thousand characters and reports success
                           while the server stores twelve hundred. #}
                        <textarea id="settings-ai-about-me"
                                  name="aboutMe"
                                  rows="4"
                                  maxlength="{{ constant('App\\Entity\\Embeddable\\AiPreferences::MAX_ABOUT_ME') }}"
                                  placeholder="{{ 'settings.ai.notes.about_me_placeholder'|trans }}"
                                  class="w-full px-3 py-2 rounded-lg text-sm bg-field border border-field text-ink
                                         focus:outline-none focus-visible:ring-2 focus-visible:ring-accent">{{ aiAboutMe }}</textarea>
                    </div>

                    <div class="space-y-1.5">
                        <label for="settings-ai-system-prompt" class="block text-xs font-medium text-ink-muted">
                            {{ 'settings.ai.notes.system_prompt_label'|trans }}
                        </label>
                        <p class="text-[11px] text-ink-faint leading-snug">{{ 'settings.ai.notes.system_prompt_hint'|trans }}</p>
                        <textarea id="settings-ai-system-prompt"
                                  name="systemPrompt"
                                  rows="3"
                                  maxlength="{{ constant('App\\Entity\\Embeddable\\AiPreferences::MAX_SYSTEM_PROMPT') }}"
                                  placeholder="{{ 'settings.ai.notes.system_prompt_placeholder'|trans }}"
                                  class="w-full px-3 py-2 rounded-lg text-sm bg-field border border-field text-ink
                                         focus:outline-none focus-visible:ring-2 focus-visible:ring-accent">{{ aiSystemPrompt }}</textarea>
                    </div>

                    <button type="submit"
                            class="inline-flex items-center justify-center h-9 px-4 rounded-lg text-sm font-medium
                                   text-accent-ink bg-accent hover:bg-accent-strong
                                   focus:outline-none focus-visible:ring-2 focus-visible:ring-accent focus-visible:ring-offset-1
                                   transition-colors duration-100 cursor-pointer">
                        {{ 'settings.ai.notes.save'|trans }}
                    </button>
                </form>
            </div>
        {% endblock %}
    {% endembed %}

    {% embed 'settings/_card.html.twig' with {
        heading:    'settings.ai.context.heading'|trans,
        subheading: 'settings.ai.context.subheading'|trans,
    } %}
        {% block body %}
            {% set segText = 'flex h-full items-center justify-center px-3 py-1.5 text-center text-[11px] leading-tight text-ink-muted
                              peer-checked:bg-accent peer-checked:text-accent-ink
                              peer-focus-visible:ring-2 peer-focus-visible:ring-inset peer-focus-visible:ring-accent
                              transition-colors' %}

            <div class="px-4 py-3 space-y-3">
                {# Submits on change and redirects, like the clock picker: the
                   choice matters on the next draft, not on this page, so there
                   is no fragment small enough to be worth swapping back. #}
                <form method="post" action="{{ path('app_settings_ai_context') }}" data-turbo="false"
                      data-controller="ui--auto-submit">
                    <input type="hidden" name="_token" value="{{ csrf_token('settings-ai-context') }}">

                    <div class="grid grid-flow-col auto-cols-fr rounded-pane border border-line overflow-hidden"
                         role="radiogroup" aria-label="{{ 'settings.ai.context.heading'|trans }}">
                        {% for depth in ['none', 'message', 'thread'] %}
                            <label class="cursor-pointer">
                                <input type="radio" name="depth" class="peer sr-only"
                                       value="{{ depth }}"
                                       data-action="change->ui--auto-submit#submit"
                                       data-ai-context-depth="{{ depth }}"
                                    {{ aiReplyContext.value == depth ? 'checked' : '' }}>
                                <span class="{{ segText }}">
                                    {{ ('settings.ai.context.' ~ depth)|trans }}
                                </span>
                            </label>
                        {% endfor %}
                    </div>
                </form>

                {# The hint belongs to the CHOSEN value rather than listing all
                   three, because the thing worth saying differs per value: one
                   of them makes "Draft a reply" refuse on an empty composer,
                   and the other two only cost time. #}
                <p class="text-[11px] text-ink-faint leading-snug">
                    {{ ('settings.ai.context.' ~ aiReplyContext.value ~ '_hint')|trans }}
                </p>

                {#
                What each feature is actually given, in plain words.

                Here because the commonest question about any of this is "why
                did it not know that", and the answer is nearly always that the
                model was handed the first screen of a message rather than the
                whole of it. Only the features that are actually running are
                listed — a line about search on an install where search is off
                explains nothing.
                #}
                <div class="pt-3 border-t border-line">
                    <h3 class="text-[11px] font-semibold uppercase tracking-wide text-ink-faint">
                        {{ 'settings.ai.reads.heading'|trans }}
                    </h3>
                    <ul class="mt-1.5 space-y-1 text-[11px] text-ink-faint leading-snug">
                        {% for feature in aiFeatures %}
                            {% if feature.adminOn and feature.enabled %}
                                <li>{{ ('settings.ai.reads.' ~ feature.key)|trans }}</li>
                            {% endif %}
                        {% endfor %}
                    </ul>
                </div>
            </div>
        {% endblock %}
    {% endembed %}
</div>
